<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Đổi Mới</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1986</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Doi Moi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Đổi Mới ('renovation') is the programme of economic reform adopted by the Sixth Congress of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-vietnam">Communist Party of Vietnam</a> in December 1986. It returned farming to households, legalised private business, freed most prices and opened the country to foreign investment and trade while keeping one-party rule. The reforms turned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> from an economy in crisis into one of the fastest-growing economies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and a major exporter.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/doi-moi.jpg" alt="Đổi Mới" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tokeisan at Vietnamese Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khu_trung_t%C3%A2m_th%C3%A0nh_ph%E1%BB%91_H%E1%BB%93_Ch%C3%AD_Minh,_nh%C3%ACn_t%E1%BB%AB_ph%C3%ADa_qu%E1%BA%ADn_2.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
